      "writtenOn": "2022-03-11T05:26:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So chipset_reset is a function in the legacy API (ec/include/chipset.h) that gets called to actually reset the AP.\nSo this is shimmed into ap_power_reset in chromium:3515426\n\nThis is different from the legacy HOOK_CHIPSET_RESET (or the new AP_POWER_RESET), which is a notification that the CPU has been reset.\nAnd yes, I see that shim/src/espi.c there is espi_chipset_reset, and in chromium:3518465 this get converted to use the ap_power_event.\nIn the legacy EC code, there only place that calls hook_notify on HOOK_CHIPSET_RESET is the espi devices, so this seems OK.\nI can\u0027t see anywhere in the legacy power sequence code that sends HOOK_CHIPSET_RESET as a notification.",
      "parentUuid": "f0933a9d_fbaa68b6",
