      "writtenOn": "2022-03-11T05:50:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ESPI_BUS_RESET is different, not the reset I meant here.\nI\u0027m wondering how we get chipset reset notification, like EC \"apreset\", or AP \"reboot\". ESPI_BUS_EVENT_VWIRE_RECEIVED signals VW channels like ESPI_VWIRE_SIGNAL_SLP_S3/S4/S5 has event, and ESPI_VWIRE_SIGNAL_PLTRST is one of the channel too. I know for sure ESPI_VWIRE_SIGNAL_PLTRST is signaled when I do \"apreset\" or AP \"reboot\". My understanding is ap_pwrseq will notify modules who registers SOC reset/or platform reset(not sure which is the right name) by ESPI_VWIRE_SIGNAL_PLTRST signaling.\nIn Shim zephyr code, chipset reset hook never happen even \"aprest\" or AP \"reboot\". maybe because it doesn\u0027t break any functionality so not noticed.\nMy point is if ap_pwrseq is the right place to send SOC reset notification, then we need to consider add the handling here.\nIf Keith can confirm this will be good.",
